The glob view strips doc comment markers (`///`, `//!`) and drops marker-only lines, the same way file mode prints them.
The TypeScript build cleaned glob view headers separately and printed `/ Triple.` and a double space here.
== args
input
== file input/doc.ts
/// Triple.
//
//! Bang.
export const x = 1;
== stdout
glob view: input
Includes only headers per file.
For file-level outlines, use `outln [FILE]...`.
input/doc.ts: Triple. Bang.
